From b0a52c1c0dc53f1e3f5579783b7363eead0e2d3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 09:08:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/43] test(chexc): escape hatch, cast targets by level,
 'resume throwing', '...' placement, warn-level override resolution

One test per rule of this round, plus the regression the std link failure earned:
'warn_override_resolution.cj' builds and RUNS a program whose implementation exceeds the
interface's list in both shapes -- declared and inferred -- and calls it through an F-bounded
type parameter, which is where a call left on the abstract member would have no body behind it.
Compiling it is not enough to catch that; the test runs the binary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
